@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix tgs: <http://example.org/tgs#> .
@prefix thinkr: <http://example.org/thinkr#> .

<http://example.org/tgs#> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <http://example.org/thinkr#> ;
    rdfs:comment "Imports tgs-core for Protege compatibility — editing this file alone will resolve thinkr: classes/properties via the catalog file."@en .

#############################################
# ADDED 2026-08-13 — a new class distinct from thinkr:Concept, raised
# by MJSullivan while testing the Concept/Subject classification logic
# against a real case: the AMOC (Atlantic Meridional Overturning
# Circulation). thinkr:Concept's own definition is specifically "a term
# or idea from Nate Hagens' Great Simplification framework" — his OWN
# analytical frameworks/reframings (Rebuildables, Shortfall Risk,
# Scenario Thinking) or substantive theories he treats as central to his
# argument even when not his own (Terror Management Theory). AMOC is
# neither — it's a real, independently-existing physical system Hagens
# hosts EXPERT GUESTS to discuss as evidence, not an idea he originates
# or reframes. thinkr:Subject was also considered and rejected: the
# existing Subject taxonomy (EROIAndEnergyQuality, EcologyAndEnvironment,
# etc.) sits at a consistently broader topic-area granularity — AMOC is
# one clear notch more specific than any existing Subject, a
# granularity mismatch, not a fit.
#
# Confirmed via real evidence, not a single passing mention, before
# minting: THREE separate episodes touch this — TGS_124 ("Oceanic
# Slowdown: Decoding the AMOC," a full episode with climate physicist
# Levke Caesar, Potsdam Institute), TGS_105 (Leon Simons, a second
# dedicated AMOC episode, found via TGS_207's own cross-reference), and
# TGS_207 itself, which explicitly cross-references both. This is what
# justified building a genuinely new class rather than folding it into
# an existing Concept's prose (the treatment given to less-recurring
# examples like ice sheets/soil systems in Concept.ComplexSystemsThinking
# — worth revisiting those as EarthSystemComponent individuals too, once
# a similar multi-episode case is confirmed for either, not assumed).
#
# DELIBERATELY DEFERRED, not done in this pass: bootstrapping Levke
# Caesar and Leon Simons as real Personas, and TGS_124/TGS_105 as real
# Episode individuals — MJSullivan's own explicit scoping choice,
# treating this as "design the class, mint AMOC only" first.
#############################################

thinkr:EarthSystemComponent a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf thinkr:Concept ;
    rdfs:comment "A real, macro-scale, physical component of Earth's climate/ecological system (e.g. the AMOC, an ice sheet, a major biome), discussed within Hagens' TGS framework — he cites it as evidence, typically via expert guests who study it directly, rather than originating or reframing the idea himself. FOLDED under thinkr:Concept 2026-08-13 (was initially built as a fully separate sibling class the same day) — per MJSullivan's explicit direction, once thinkr:Concept itself was revised into an explicit umbrella (see thinkr:Concept's own rdfs:comment and the new thinkr:HagensConcept subclass). Deliberately NOT a thinkr:HagensConcept — AMOC and its siblings are exactly the kind of externally-originated, adopted-not-authored content that subclass exists to exclude."@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Earth System Component"@en .

tgs:EarthSystemComponent.AMOC a thinkr:EarthSystemComponent, thinkr:Concept, owl:NamedIndividual ;
    dcterms:subject tgs:Subject.EcologyAndEnvironment ;
    skos:prefLabel "Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation"@en ;
    skos:definition "The major ocean current system that transports warm water northward and cold water southward through the Atlantic, regulating temperature between the Northern and Southern Hemispheres — estimated to have slowed by roughly 15% over recent decades, with real scientific concern (per the tgs:Work.GlobalTippingPointsReport2025 and multiple TGS episodes) about a potential collapse and its cascading effects on regional/global climate systems."@en ;
    thinkr:hasAlternateTerm [ a thinkr:AlternateTerm ;
        thinkr:hasAlternateTermType tgs:AlternateTermType.ExactMatch, tgs:AlternateTermType.Abbreviation ;
        skos:prefLabel "AMOC"@en ;
        skos:scopeNote "Following the same standing convention as tgs:Concept.EnergyReturnOnInvestment: full expanded form is canonical (prefLabel + IRI), the abbreviation goes into the AlternateTerm." ] ;
    skos:scopeNote "Confirmed via real search 2026-08-13 (thegreatsimplification.com/episode/124-levke-caesar, and TGS_207's own cross-reference to both TGS_124 and TGS_105) — NOT yet linked via thinkr:discusses to any Episode individual, since TGS_124/TGS_105 don't exist as Episode individuals in this graph yet (see this file's own header note on what was deliberately deferred). Real next step once those episodes are bootstrapped: link both via thinkr:discusses, now that its range has been widened to include thinkr:EarthSystemComponent."@en .
